onemedia repair <in> <out> [--reference <file>]   rebuild indexes, counts and durations of a damaged Matroska/WebM, AVI, MP4/MOV/3GP, fragmented MP4 or MPEG-TS file into a new file;
                     an MP4/MOV/3GP cut off before its movie box is rebuilt from its media data (--reference gives the codec setup);
                     exit 0 when repaired or nothing to repair (the output is then a byte-identical copy), 1 when only partly repaired, 2 when nothing could be recovered

